# Error Diagnostics Standards

## Context
- When implementing error handling
- When logging errors in critical operations
- When debugging complex operations

## Requirements
- Include contextual data in error messages
- Log both error details and relevant state
- Provide component-specific error information
- Track error codes and their meanings
- Include system state in error logs
- Log relevant metrics with errors
- Implement hierarchical error logging
- Include operation metadata in error context
- Preserve error chain information

## Examples
<example>
```rust
error!(
    "Proof verification failed - Details:\n\
     - Error: {:?}\n\
     - Input count: {}\n\
     - Total proof size: {} bytes\n\
     - Component hashes:\n\
       * proof_a: {}\n\
       * proof_b: {}\n\
     - First input preview: {}",
    e,
    input_count,
    proof_size,
    hex::encode(hash_a),
    hex::encode(hash_b),
    hex::encode(first_input)
);
```
Provides comprehensive error context with relevant state information
</example>

<example type="invalid">
```rust
error!("Verification failed: {:?}", e);
```
Lacks context and state information needed for debugging
</example> 